<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24579" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-tractātus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		2. in-tracto, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>not handled</i> or <i>managed</i>,
				<i>untamed</i>, <i>wild;
			untried</i>, <i>unattempted</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equus,</span>”
				<i>unbroken</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Lael. 19, 68</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">decor,</span>”
				<i>wild</i>, <i>natural</i>, <i>simple</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Grat. Cyn. 134</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lanae,</span>”
				<i>not carded</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
						Aur. Acut. 3, 5, 57</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne quid intractatum scelerisve dolive fuisset,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 8, 206</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
